cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FlahaX, please cite it as below, and credit the data sources listed under references."
title: "FlahaX: plant-nutrient chemistry engine for fertilizer formulation and delivery planning"
abstract: >-
  FlahaX turns a water analysis, a crop formula and the fertilizers at hand
  into a batch: the fertilizer recipe, the calculated pH, the acid-adjusted
  recipe and the A/B stock tanks to prepare. Growers and agronomists use the
  interactive `flahax mix` command; developers use the Python API. Underneath,
  it chooses fertilizer grams by non-negative least squares so the crop
  formula is met after the water's contribution; models the solution with
  fertilizer-specific aqueous equilibrium chemistry (speciation, saturation
  and pH) at the water's measured pH; plans the acid or base dose to a
  target pH with the reagent's nutrients counted; groups products into two
  concentrate tanks and checks their solubility; and records units, sources
  and hashes for audit. Materials are defined by formula, ions or label
  analysis. Chemistry is checked against PHREEQC 3.8.6. Pure Python, no
  runtime dependencies.
